    "pages": "p. 1 (frequently used), p. 2 (output registers, A/B lists, counter A), p. 3 (counters B and C)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "No direct Red Lion download of this table was found; the link is an unaltered copy of the Red Lion table (LP0930A) on a distributor's file host.",
    "32-bit values are a Hi word register followed by a Lo word register (ABCD); limits such as -999999999 show they are signed.",
    "Counts, rates, setpoints and count loads are the displayed digits without the decimal point (the A/B list section says 1 = 1 in the least significant digit, decimal point disregarded).",
    "Scale factor scaling (1 = 0.00001, decimal point fixed) is printed in the A/B list section for the same parameter and applied here to the active-list copies.",
    "Left out: A/B list copies 40041-40100, rate, user input, setpoint output, display and port settings later in the table (the serial port registers 40482-40490 are described under integration)."
  ],
